[1m[38;5;231mWhat makes a task one a user "cares about"?[0m

[38;5;153m❯[39m [38;5;246m1.[39m [38;5;153mInvolvement + manual override (Recommended)[39m
     [38;5;246mAuto-subscribed when you create, are assigned, or comment on a task — plus explicit watch/unwatch to opt in or out.
[39m     [38;5;246mNeeds a subscriptions table. Covers both failure modes; the standard for good reason.[39m
  [38;5;246m2.[39m Assignment only
     [38;5;246mYou hear about tasks assigned to you, nothing else. Simplest possible model, no extra table, no settings UI. But [39m
     [38;5;246mcreators hear nothing about their own tasks, and nobody can follow work they aren't doing.[39m
  [38;5;246m3.[39m Explicit watching only
     [38;5;246mNothing is automatic; you star tasks to follow them. Total user control and no unwanted noise, but relies on people
[39m     [38;5;246mremembering to subscribe — in practice the important notifications get missed.[39m
  [38;5;246m4.[39m List/project membership
     [38;5;246mTasks live in lists; you're notified about everything in lists you belong to. Good if work is naturally grouped and
[39m     [38;5;246mteams are small, but gets noisy fast as lists grow and offers no per-task control.[39m
  [38;5;246m5. Type something.[39m
